 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "MetalMachAdvisor ⊣ Metallurgy Machinery Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS
 COORDINATION actor for ISIC 2823 (Manufacture of machinery for
 metallurgy) -- rolling mills, casting machinery and metal-processing
 plant equipment, distinct from siblings 2812 [fluid power equipment]/
 2815 [ovens, furnaces and furnace burners]/2819 [other general-purpose
 machinery] -- this build picks ONE concrete illustrative product line,
 documented plainly in the README: rolling-mill and casting-machinery
 manufacturing (rolling-mill stands, continuous casters, die-casting
 machines, extrusion presses, forging presses, wire-drawing machines)
 -- fabrication and assembly/test-bench lines producing finished
 metallurgy-processing machinery -- not direct fabrication/assembly-
 line-equipment control authority and not machinery-safety
 certification authority (e.g. EU Machinery Directive 2006/42/EC CE
 conformity marking or ANSI B11.19 machine-safeguarding conformity
 marking). Four ops (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance`
 / `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Governor checks elaborate this blueprint's four HARD
 invariants: propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed
 proposal-effect allowlist (no direct fabrication/assembly-line-
 equipment control), permanent equipment-actuate block, permanent
 machinery-safety-certification-authority block (this actor never
 self-issues a CE/ANSI-B11.19 machinery-safety conformity mark),
 independent equipment verification/registration before maintenance
 scheduling, independent batch verification/registration before
 shipment coordination, independent shipment-quantity recompute
 against the batch's own logged production quantity, double-schedule
 guard, product-type validation, load-test plausibility validation,
 and defect-rate plausibility validation. Safety-concern flagging
 (equipment-safety/structural-integrity/quality-defect concern) ALWAYS
 escalates to a human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch` is the
 only op eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when
 governor-clean."}
